From c9840f18ab8cbb3918bddcfb92a8547949ad5aaa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 17:53:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] A type=text with no font kills the client, not the server

The 22 XP-lock buttons draw no text, so they were given no font=. PackShared's
nameToFont returns -1 for a missing one, p1(-1) is the byte 255, and Component.decode
does `com.font = fonts[font]` on an array of FOUR - so the client dies inside
Component.unpack with "loaderror Unpacking interfaces 95" before the login screen.

There is no server-side symptom whatsoever: the pack builds clean and the world comes
up. The guide buttons these copy their geometry from carry font=p12_full and
shadowed=yes, which was the clue sitting in the file.

rs2check rule 20 now reads every .if in the repo: a type=text must name a font the
packer knows, and a component must name a type it knows. It is in --selftest with its
own fixture, so it is proven to go red, and a repo-wide run says these 22 were the only
ones.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
